cff-version: 1.2.0
title: CellLabel
message: >-
  If you use CellLabel in work you publish, please cite it using the
  metadata in this file.
type: software
abstract: >-
  A macOS, Windows and Linux application for counting cells in Olympus and
  Evident cellSens slide scans. It opens .vsi and .ets pyramids directly,
  without conversion, and supports both manual click-counting and a
  node-based detection pipeline whose output a person reviews before it is
  committed. Counts, outlines and per-point coordinates export as CSV.
authors:
  - family-names: Buckwalter-Chiang
    given-names: Max
version: 1.2.1
date-released: '2026-11-11'
url: 'https://celllabel.com'
repository-artifact: 'https://github.com/mbc210/celllabel-releases'
license-url: >-
  https://github.com/mbc210/celllabel-releases/blob/main/LICENSE
keywords:
  - cell counting
  - histology
  - fluorescence microscopy
  - slide scanning
  - cellSens
  - stereology
  - image analysis
  - neuroanatomy
# Add the Zenodo DOI here once the deposit exists, as:
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
references:
